WEBVTT

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.840
<i>In some sense, they are like mirrors.</i>

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Neither machines nor dolls,</i>

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:17.040
<i>reflecting the love that they receive from their
owners, they grow up.</i>

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.400
<i>You are a...</i>

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.080
<i>...Hybrid Child.</i>

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.320
<i>l said that if it wasn't Hazuki, it was no good.</i>

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.580
So hot....

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:35.400
No good! I just got into the mood to study
but in this heat, any will to study disappears!

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.820
Hazuki...

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.390
Kotarou-sama,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.680
I don't think you should be blaming your laziness
on the weather.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.060
Your results are bad enough already. At this rate,
your rankings are definitely going to drop further.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.440
Even though you are so unreliable you are still
considered the heir of the lzumi family,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.800
so please be more aware of that fact.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.230
Yes! yes!

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.090
Just one "yes" will suffice.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.680
Yeah yeah, I'm sorry that the heir of the family
has to be such an idiot!

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:05.820
Enough with the talking back.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:10.290
If you feel so bad about it just once is good enough.
Try to take an exam without failing.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.600
After that, feel free to complain about me
as much as you like.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.140
You...

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.800
<i>I picked up Hakuzi from the garbage dump
when I was eight.</i>

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.820
I thought that he was just a doll,

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.580
<i>but it seems like he's this product called
a "Hybrid Child".</i>

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:36.280
<i>Right now, it's enjoying popularity amongst
private circles of rich, middle aged men.</i>

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.750
<i>In other words, it's that...</i>

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.270
<i>dependent on the love it receives,</i>

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.440
<i>it can be brought up according to the owner's wishes.</i>

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.280
<i>That's the height of men's fantasies.</i>

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:03.610
<i>I haven't thought of such perverted things though,</i>

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.840
<i>Besides, Hazuki is a man.</i>

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.010
<i>Even though it's just bringing this up,</i>

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.950
<i>the "Hybrid Child" is not that easy to handle.</i>

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.490
<i>That's why</i>

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.280
<i>when Hazuki started to move</i>

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.590
<i>I was extremely happy.</i>

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.980
<i>Just like a duckling, he followed me
everywhere I went</i>

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.740
<i>and listened to everything I said.</i>

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.500
<i>He was obedient</i>

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.770
<i>and honest.</i>

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:45.730
<i>Despite that...</i>

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.740
Why did it end up like this!?

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.370
Kotarou, here and here...

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.820
Ah... you got this wrong too.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.540
Where did I go wrong!?

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.640
How can you make such a simple mistake?

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.660
Please read the question carefully from the start.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.230
<i>Before I knew it, he grew taller than me.</i>

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.870
You're making all those mistakes because you don't
read the questions carefully.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.590
By the way, don't you feel hot wearing that?

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.120
I feel all sweaty just looking at you.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:12.790
I'm okay.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:17.340
Unlike humans, I have a function which regulates
my body temperature.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:19.370
See?

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.090
So cold...

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.810
When my temperature exceeds 25 degree Celsius,
it will make adjustments automatically.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.570
Being a human sure is inconvenient...

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:35.380
Hazuki!

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:37.330
Yes?

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:38.670
Strip!

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.500
W-Wait! Kotarou!

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.440
Stop!

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.130
Strip! Take everything off!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:43.500
Please stop!

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.100
No! Kotarou! I have no such intentions...

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.180
W-Wait! Kotarou!

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.240
This feels so good!

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.260
I feel refreshed!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.580
Why didn't I find out about this before?

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:06.860
If I knew about this, I wouldn't have suffered from
heat exhaustion every summer.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:09.760
He's an idiot.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:14.430
<i>Why is my owner such an idiot?</i>

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.700
<i>Recently, the weird headaches I've been having
are definitely his fault.</i>

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.650
Hey, let go of me.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.100
Haven't you cooled down enough?

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.290
<i>Goodness, this person...</i>

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.740
<i>Nothing has changed since 10 years ago.</i>

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.490
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.790
<i>The day I was picked up by Kotarou
was a hot day like today too.</i>

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:04.020
<i>Before I came to this house, I was abandoned twice.</i>

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:09.940
<i>The third time, I was brought home by Kotarou, and
thrown away by the people of this family thrice.</i>

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.990
<i>Despite all that, Kotarou</i>

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.300
<i>came back and took me home each time.</i>

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:20.820
<i>Always...</i>

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.640
<i>We're always together.</i>

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:31.810
<i>Well, even though I owe him a debt,</i>

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:34.850
<i>I have no intention of spoiling him at all.</i>

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:39.480
<i>No, even now I might be spoiling him too much.</i>

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.130
<i>The Izumi family that has been around for 50 years
is the noblest of the noble families.</i>

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.350
<i>If the family head is like this, then this
household will definitely crumble.</i>

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:51.970
<i>He needs to be at least groomed to be on par
with others.</i>

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:53.970
<i>I'll help him.</i>

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.620
You can continue to sleep.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:08.740
Your brain probably won't work under the
heat anyway.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.960
I had an amazing dream.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.020
What kind?

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.060
I was buried in a sea of shaved ice.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.600
It felt so good!

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:19.330
So cool! This is bad! So cool!

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.080
I'm taking back those words, wake up immediately!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.940
We're going to study! Come on! Hurry up!

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:24.410
I can't!

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.410
If I don't sleep now, I'll die!

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:28.630
So annoying!

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:31.500
You know, you get irritated too easily.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:34.720
It's not good to have a high blood pressure...

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.190
<i>Whose fault do you think it is!?</i>

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.040
<i>That's right, this is all Kotarou's fault.</i>

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:42.180
<i>Lately, it seems that I haven't been feeling well.</i>

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.690
<i>I feel sluggish, breathless and dizzy.</i>

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.760
Hey! Goodness! You really are...

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.970
How many times must I say it before you get it!?

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:09.580
Hazuki!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:40.120
You're Kuroda, right?

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.060
Hey!

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:48.290
I'm asking you a question, how about answering?

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:50.450
Hey!

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.680
You're the one who made the Hybrid Child, right?

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:02.320
Take a look at him.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:04.040
He collapsed suddenly.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.010
Something might be wrong with him.

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:08.040
Where did you get that from?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:11.320
It's not something a brat like you should own.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:13.410
Where did you steal it from?

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.100
Don't say such rude things!

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.960
I may not look like it, but I'm the 16th head
of the Izumi family.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:19.620
Oh...

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:24.390
So you're a rich brat who has it easy because you're
riding on your family's coattails?

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.900
He didn't steal,

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:30.720
rather, I was picked up by him.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:34.820
Hazuki, we're leaving!

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.640
A guy like him must be a fake, how ridiculous!

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.900
Kotarou, he's the one.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:45.720
I wouldn't forget the human who created me.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:48.500
Take your clothes off.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.640
Serial number 0001.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:38.470
Hey, isn't this the first model?

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.340
You can't find such an antique anywhere else now.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:43.860
Look at this,

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.750
the joints between the parts have completely
disappeared.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.000
His skin has transformed to almost like a human's.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.720
Amazing.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:54.760
This is my first time seeing a transformation
of this extent too.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.810
This is an important research material, so we can
perform an autopsy...

00:10:58.810 --> 00:10:59.840
Stop kidding!

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:01.330
Don't joke around!

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.720
I brought him here to be repaired, you can't--

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:04.680
This can't be repaired.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:06.000
Why!?

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:08.020
If you created him, you should be able to repair him!

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:08.720
Impossible.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:09.570
Why!?

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:12.300
Listen, Young Master.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:16.730
Hybrid Child is neither a machine nor a human.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:20.730
It's not something which can be returned to its
normal state after a change of parts.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.540
What are you doing!?

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.650
Relax. He doesn't feel pain...

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:30.100
...because he isn't human.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.050
Try smelling this.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.030
This isn't an issue of repairing him.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:41.730
Its his lifespan.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:45.470
Think of his entire body as one single cell...

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:49.750
...that has already started decaying from the inside.

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.240
Don't joke around!

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.520
I don't get what you're saying at all!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.310
You aren't very smart.

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:00.430
Repair him!

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.940
If you want money, I'll pay! How much do you want?

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:05.260
Money huh...

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:12.060
Then, 5 million yen.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:14.920
You must be kidding!

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.060
Isn't that more than the national budget?

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:19.590
So you do have some boring knowledge.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:23.640
If you have that much money, how about
buying another Hybrid Child?

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:26.180
The 3000 model is out right now.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.740
They've become much easier to handle.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.490
I don't need something like that,

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.200
I only need Hazuki!

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.510
Repair him!

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:39.350
Or is that it? You don't have the confidence
to repair him?

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:43.040
Don't kids these days even know how to ask
for a favor properly?

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:44.850
Wait! Please wait!

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:47.010
If there's anything I can do I'll do it!

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:51.170
If its not Hazuki, it's no good!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:04.660
I understand.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.220
Then, go get me the "Droplet of the Moon".

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:11.950
"Droplet of the Moon"?

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:20.510
It must be buried 90 degrees below the midpoint between
the church on the beach and the Northern Star.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.210
You should know this already,

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:26.560
that it's meaningless if the owner doesn't find it himself.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:31.360
If we use that to create a cultured solution
maybe he can be repaired.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.140
By the way, what's that?

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:39.190
You're the owner of a Hybrid Child, yet you
don't even know what that is?

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:41.090
Of course I know!

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.420
Understood, "Droplet of the Moon", right?

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:51.340
<i>Droplet of the Moon, Droplet of the Moon,</i>

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:53.350
<i>Droplet of the Moon...</i>

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:59.010
<i>Hazuki can hang on for one more week only.</i>

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:04.560
<i>From its name, it's probably small enough to be
rolled on one's palm.</i>

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:07.360
<i>I have to find it.</i>

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:11.660
<i>The color is probably milky white or iridescent,</i>

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:16.250
<i>radiating the light of the moon.</i>

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.750
<i>If I can just find it quickly, Hazuki will be saved.</i>

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.840
<i>It's sitting there quietly,</i>

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.110
<i>waiting to be found.</i>

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.110
<i>If I...!</i>

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.150
<i>If I can just find it!</i>

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:40.280
In the end...

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.110
I'm at the end of my lifespan.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:48.500
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.250
You shouldn't waste your efforts.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:55.700
Since I'll have to die anyway.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.220
How ironic,

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:05.500
I've never seen you with such a serious
expression before.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:09.560
Listen,

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.530
even if I'm no longer around, you have to
pass your exams.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.760
Even though your family has the money,

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.610
find an excellent home tutor and-

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:19.200
Shut up! Be quiet!

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:23.410
Ouch!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:24.760
What's wrong?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:26.910
It's nothing.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.480
Oh look at this, your blisters have burst.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.370
That's because you're doing things you
are not used to.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.080
But besides that, you're holding the shovel weirdly.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:34.880
Leave me be!

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.710
I can't stand watching this, let me help you.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:37.340
It's fine.

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:38.450
This can't be fine.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.780
Didn't I say it's fine!?

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:40.970
Don't interfere!

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.060
Just stay aside! You're annoying!

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:48.390
Even though you're trying to save me, you'd also
beat me won't you...

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:50.390
If you're so free, then go home and sleep!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.460
This is my duty.

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:01.400
Kotarou...

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:20.840
Don't joke around, stupid.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:26.200
<i>No matter when or where,</i>

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:28.790
<i>we were always together.</i>

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.960
<i>After I'm gone from this world,</i>

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:34.700
<i>how much time will pass...</i>

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:38.060
<i>...before you forget about me?</i>

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.490
Is that idiot still digging?

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:43.400
Yes,

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.860
his family will start complaining soon
and I'll be troubled.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:50.130
Does this "Droplet of the Moon" really exist?

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:50.790
It does.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.010
I see.

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:58.980
But I didn't even say once that you can be
saved once I get a hold of it.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:02.390
He seems to be really in love with you.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:10.380
That person is the stupidest and the most useless
head in the history of the Izumi family.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:15.150
If he loses someone like me as his support,
he'll be troubled.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.520
You said you were picked up, right?

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.810
In other words, you were abandoned?

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:23.970
Yes, twice.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:25.750
No, five times.

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:31.550
It's easy to say something like "bring it up
the way you like it".

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:35.360
In reality, its harder than raising a human child.

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:39.500
Yeah. Especially because you are the first model.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.640
I probably became too troublesome,

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.430
so I got abandoned twice.

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:45.000
And then...

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.310
I got picked up by Kotarou.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:55.760
By then I was already all dirty and worn out.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.930
The people in the Izumi family kept nagging at him...

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:02.650
"Throw away that dirty thing."

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.370
They threw me out when Kotarou wasn't around.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:10.410
That happened thrice.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:23.920
So, you're saying he retrieved you all three times?

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.390
What a strange brat.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:30.660
Will normal people go that far?

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:33.910
What Kotarou said was...

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:37.410
<i>I don't want a new one!</i>

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.510
<i>All I need is Hazuki!</i>

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:41.940
<i>If it's not Hazuki, it's no good!</i>

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.020
I looked very lonely.

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:48.870
Five years.

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:54.360
It took me 5 years to start moving,

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:57.340
and another year and a half to start speaking.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.250
He's an idiot.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:13.380
Don't misunderstand.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:16.750
You are merely an object, not human.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.810
Don't misunderstand and start having
romantic feelings for humans.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:22.960
Romantic feelings?

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.060
Like?

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:25.380
Love?

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:28.420
This isn't one of those momentary, fleeting sentiments!

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:34.710
This body, voice, heart...

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:41.660
...are all things that Kotarou gave me.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.140
My everything...

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.360
...belongs to Kotarou!

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:04.930
Time's up.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:13.440
I'm not afraid... of dying.

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:16.070
I'm just worried...

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.320
...when I'm gone...

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.050
...will he be able to live properly?

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:24.670
He's naive,

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:26.480
has bad memory,

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:28.220
is rude,

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:29.870
and isn't smart.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:31.650
But...

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.820
He's kinder than anyone else.

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:38.560
More than anyone else in this world,
he cares for me.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:49.540
Hazuki,

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:52.020
I'm sorry.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.510
I couldn't find it.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.300
I tried my best to search,

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:00.050
but couldn't find it at all.

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:03.600
Sorry!

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:05.050
I'm really sorry!

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:08.020
I hate myself, I hate myself!

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:10.940
Why am I always like this?

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:15.810
Why can't I do anything for you?

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:33.240
See? Isn't he an idiot?

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:04.730
Yes?

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:08.020
Kotarou-sama, you have a call.

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:09.560
Who's it from?

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:13.070
It's from a man who said "just put him on the phone."

00:22:13.470 --> 00:22:15.170
Got it. I'll speak to him.

00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:20.450
Hello, Kotarou speaking, may I know who-

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:23.850
Wow, you sure changed a lot in an year.

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:26.020
You--You're Kuroda?

00:22:26.420 --> 00:22:29.200
I guess you can only change so much
within an year, right?

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:31.570
What is it all of a sudden?

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:36.280
Do you remember excavating the entire beach to find the "Droplet of the Moon" last year?

00:22:36.690 --> 00:22:37.570
What about it?

00:22:37.640 --> 00:22:39.270
That was all a lie.

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:42.470
WHAT!?

00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:45.930
I just had to make a conceited brat do all that.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.000
What did you say? Don't joke with me!

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:50.190
Shouldn't there be a limit to what you can do
and what you can't?

00:22:50.320 --> 00:22:51.870
Do you know what sort of feelings I had then-

00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:52.360
What's why...

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:55.270
First of all, I've returned what's yours.

00:22:55.510 --> 00:22:59.480
But since that and this are two different things,
I got him to bring along a bill.

00:22:59.510 --> 00:23:00.700
Huh? What?

00:23:01.100 --> 00:23:02.220
What did you say?

00:23:02.260 --> 00:23:04.210
It caused me a lot of trouble.

00:23:04.260 --> 00:23:08.050
Well, you can thank me. I gave you a 20% discount.

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:08.640
Bye then.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.250
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:11.410
Hey Kuroda!

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:15.360
What was that about?

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.180
Even though I'm trying so hard to forget about him...

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:30.910
Although its a 20% discount it's still 4 million yen.

00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:34.860
Every single one of you only knows
how to cause trouble.

00:23:36.410 --> 00:23:37.640
Hazuki!

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:52.150
<i>It took 5 years just to start moving.</i>

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:54.910
<i>And another year and a half to start talking.</i>

00:23:57.390 --> 00:23:58.650
<i>When summer comes,</i>

00:23:59.790 --> 00:24:00.790
<i>I'll remember...</i>

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:10.660
Tsumetai sono taion wo kanjiteru

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:10.660
Feeling the coolness of your body temperature

00:24:10.660 --> 00:24:15.270
Kasanaru kage ni mo himitsu madotte

00:24:10.660 --> 00:24:15.270
Even the overlapping shadows hide secrets

00:24:24.590 --> 00:24:28.450
Yurari, Yurari

00:24:24.590 --> 00:24:28.450
Swaying, swaying,

00:24:29.210 --> 00:24:33.110
Kokoro ga yureteru

00:24:29.210 --> 00:24:33.110
My heart is swaying

00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:42.890
Zutto onaji basho wo motomete

00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:42.890
Always seeking for the same place

00:24:43.500 --> 00:24:47.730
Kagami no youni utsushidashite

00:24:43.500 --> 00:24:47.730
Reflecting like a mirror

00:24:47.730 --> 00:24:52.400
Tashikametai setsuna no kioku

00:24:47.730 --> 00:24:52.400
The sad memories I want to confirm

00:24:52.400 --> 00:25:01.340
Sono karada katachi sae futari no mono dakara

00:24:52.400 --> 00:25:01.340
because the silhouette of that body belongs to the two of us

00:25:02.690 --> 00:25:07.520
Tsumetai sono taion wo kanjite

00:25:02.690 --> 00:25:07.520
Feeling the coolness of your body temperature

00:25:07.520 --> 00:25:12.120
Chiisai hana he te omoitakushite

00:25:07.520 --> 00:25:12.120
Entrusting our feelings to little flowers

00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:15.220
Tsuki no hikari no shita

00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:15.220
Beneath the moonlight

00:25:15.260 --> 00:25:21.090
Doko made mo yukimashou issho ni

00:25:15.260 --> 00:25:21.090
I'll go anywhere with you, together

00:25:23.560 --> 00:25:25.910
Tsunaida te ni,

00:25:23.560 --> 00:25:25.910
Our intertwined fingers

00:25:28.370 --> 00:25:31.980
Nagarekomu koro

00:25:28.370 --> 00:25:31.980
the time which flows by

00:25:37.880 --> 00:25:38.830
<i>This person said,</i>

00:25:40.100 --> 00:25:41.330
<i>that if it wasn't me,</i>

00:25:42.170 --> 00:25:43.540
<i>it was no good.</i>

